IMPORT prelude

-- Civil Liability Act 1936 (SA) -- the dates and small arithmetic, in one small module. It uses only the built-in date
-- functions (DATE_FROM_DMY, DATE_SERIAL, DATE_FROM_SERIAL, DATE_DAY, DATE_MONTH, DATE_YEAR) and FLOOR, not the daydate
-- library.
--
-- READINGS (forks F1 and F2 in NOTES.md; the text does not say):
--   * "within three years after the death", "within six months after the death": the same day of the month that many
--     months later, or that month's last day where it is shorter (29 February 2024 plus 3 years is 28 February 2027).
--   * "to the nearest multiple of $10": an amount exactly half-way ($5 over a multiple) goes up.
--
-- Based on content from the South Australian Legislation website, as collected by the Open Australian Legal Corpus on
-- 10 March 2025 (unofficial, possibly out of date). CC BY 4.0. BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice.

§ `Dates and arithmetic for the Civil Liability Act 1936`

GIVEN d IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the date` d m y MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY d m y

GIVEN `the first day` IS A DATE, `the second day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the first day` `is on or before` `the second day` IF DATE_SERIAL `the first day` AT MOST DATE_SERIAL `the second day`

GIVEN `the first day` IS A DATE, `the second day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the first day` `is before` `the second day` IF DATE_SERIAL `the first day` LESS THAN DATE_SERIAL `the second day`

GIVEN `the first day` IS A DATE, `the second day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days from` `the first day` `to` `the second day` MEANS DATE_SERIAL `the second day` MINUS DATE_SERIAL `the first day`

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER, b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the smaller of` a `and` b MEANS IF a AT MOST b THEN a ELSE b

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER, b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the larger of` a `and` b MEANS IF a AT LEAST b THEN a ELSE b

GIVEN m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of days in month` m `of` y MEANS
    IF m EQUALS 12
    THEN 31
    ELSE DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 (m PLUS 1) y) MINUS DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 m y)

-- Fork F1: the same day of the month n months later, or that month's last day where it is shorter.
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE, n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the day` `plus months` n MEANS
    DATE_FROM_DMY (`the smaller of` (DATE_DAY `the day`) `and` (`the number of days in month` `the new month` `of` `the new year`)) `the new month` `the new year`
    WHERE
        `the month count` MEANS (DATE_YEAR `the day` TIMES 12) PLUS (DATE_MONTH `the day` MINUS 1) PLUS n
        `the new year`    MEANS FLOOR (`the month count` DIVIDED BY 12)
        `the new month`   MEANS (`the month count` MINUS (`the new year` TIMES 12)) PLUS 1

-- Fork F2: "calculated to the nearest multiple of $10" (s 3(1) prescribed maximum and minimum; s 52(2)(d), (7)).
GIVEN x IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`to the nearest multiple of $10` x MEANS FLOOR ((x DIVIDED BY 10) PLUS 0.5) TIMES 10

-- "a percentage" reduction: x reduced by p per cent.
GIVEN x IS A NUMBER, p IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
x `reduced by per cent` p MEANS x TIMES ((100 MINUS p) DIVIDED BY 100)
